<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <EnableNETAnalyzers>true</EnableNETAnalyzers>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest</AnalysisLevel>
    <!-- NU1510: Package pruning warnings during multi-targeting (false positive for conditional references) -->
    <!-- NU5104: Allow prerelease dependencies for .NET 10 preview support -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NU1510;NU5104</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- NuGet Package Metadata -->
    <PackageId>EasyAppDev.Blazor.Store</PackageId>
    <Version>3.0.0</Version>
    <Authors>Mashrul Haque</Authors>
    <Company>EasyAppDev</Company>
    <Product>EasyAppDev.Blazor.Store</Product>
    <Description>Zustand-inspired state management for Blazor WebAssembly, Blazor Server, and MAUI Hybrid. Zero boilerplate with C# records. Features: TanStack-inspired query system, cross-tab sync, SignalR real-time collaboration, undo/redo history, optimistic updates, Redux DevTools, localStorage persistence, request deduplication, and Immer-style updates.</Description>
    <PackageTags>blazor;state-management;blazor-state;blazor-webassembly;blazor-server;maui-hybrid;zustand;fluxor-alternative;redux-devtools;signalr;cross-tab-sync;undo-redo;optimistic-updates;query-client;tanstack-query;immutable-state;csharp-records;dotnet8;dotnet9;real-time-collaboration;persistence;localstorage</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/mashrulhaque/EasyAppDev.Blazor.Store</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/mashrulhaque/EasyAppDev.Blazor.Store</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v3.0.0 - Major Reliability Release

This release fixes ~56 verified bugs found in a full-codebase audit and wires up
several previously non-functional features. It contains breaking changes.

Now actually working (previously dead code):
- Cross-tab sync now APPLIES incoming updates (receive path was never wired)
- Server sync (SignalR) connects automatically and applies remote updates
- Plugin lifecycle hooks (OnStoreCreated/OnBeforeUpdate/OnAfterUpdate/OnStoreDisposing)
- WithHistory(out history) undo/redo on the builder path
- Redux DevTools ship in the package (runtime-gated: debugger-attached or
  DevToolsOptions.Enabled = true), including time travel
- UrlSync ExcludeActions filtering
- Query client defaults (DefaultStaleTime/DefaultRetry)
- NEW: RefetchOnWindowFocus / RefetchOnReconnect for queries

Breaking changes:
- IQueryClient is now scoped (fixes cross-user cache leakage on Blazor Server)
- Persistence with EnableIntegrityCheck=true (the options-based default) now
  throws at startup unless a stable SigningKey is supplied
- Nested UpdateAsync from middleware/updaters throws (previously deadlocked)
- ActionDispatcher throws on unhandled actions (matches documented contract)
- AddTransientStore no longer registers reader/writer/observable aliases
- ServerSync protocol: signed full-state messages, 3-arg JoinDocument
- TabSync default channel name uses the full type name
- Store now disposes its middlewares (IAsyncDisposable)

Reliability highlights:
- Fixed cancellation races in Query/Mutation (stale overwrites, duplicate
  fetches/writes, a process-crash path on Blazor Server)
- Fixed sensitive-data filter corrupting persisted dictionaries and non-string
  properties; token-boundary keyword matching (ShippingAddress no longer filtered)
- Debounced persistence/tab-sync no longer block the store lock and now coalesce
- Fixed UrlSync wiping state, erasing unrelated query params, and crashing on
  page-to-page navigation; URL values now merge instead of replace
- Fixed unbounded memory growth in DiagnosticsService and QueryClient
- History grouping no longer corrupts the undo stack after Undo

v2.0.12 - Persistence Hydration Fixes (fixes #11)

Bug Fixes:
- WithPersistence(provider, options) and WithSecurePersistence() now hydrate
  state on init in WebAssembly mode (previously only WithPersistence(sp, key) did)
- Unified sync hydration path: wrapper format, HMAC signature verification,
  state validation, and TransformOnLoad are applied consistently across all
  WithPersistence overloads
- Hydration errors now log to ILogger and Console.Error (was silent
  Debug.WriteLine in Release WASM)
- New public API: PersistenceMiddleware.TryLoadStateSync() for advanced scenarios

v2.0.9 - LLM-Friendly Documentation

New Features:
- Added llms.txt and llms-full.txt following llmstxt.org specification
- Enables AI agents to navigate documentation more effectively

v2.0.8 - AsyncData Refetch Support

New Features:
- Added IsFetching property to AsyncData for tracking fetch operations
- Added IsRefetching computed property (true when refetching while data exists)
- Added ToLoadingPreserved() method for stale-while-revalidate pattern
- Preserves existing data during background refetches

v2.0.7 - URL Sync (Experimental)

New Features:
- UrlSyncStoreComponent&lt;T&gt; base class for bidirectional URL-state synchronization
- [AutoSyncWithQuery] attribute for zero-boilerplate query parameter binding
- Fluent IUrlSyncBuilder API for manual configuration
- 3-layer circular update prevention
- Configurable debounce and navigation modes (Replace/Push)
- Convention-based auto-discovery of URL mappings

v2.0.6 - Cache Invalidation Convenience Methods

New Features:
- Added convenience wrapper methods in StoreComponentWithUtilities for cache invalidation:
  - InvalidateCachedResult(key) - Remove specific cached entry
  - InvalidateCachedResultsByPrefix(prefix) - Remove entries by prefix
  - ClearCachedResults() - Clear all cached results
- Improved discoverability of cache management APIs

v2.0.5 - ExecuteCachedAsync
- Added ExecuteCachedAsync for deduplicated async actions with caching
- Deduplicates both fetch AND state updates across concurrent callers

v2.0.4 - Bug Fixes &amp; Stability
(See previous release notes for full changelog)
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="EasyAppDev.Blazor.Store.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- .NET 8 Package References -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.SignalR.Client" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Collections.Immutable" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="8.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- .NET 9 Package References (System.Collections.Immutable is built-in) -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net9.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="9.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.SignalR.Client" Version="9.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="9.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="9.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- .NET 10 Package References (System.Collections.Immutable is built-in) -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.0-preview.1.25120.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.SignalR.Client" Version="10.0.0-preview.1.25120.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0-preview.1.25080.5" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0-preview.1.25080.5" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Note: SecureStoreHubBase requires ASP.NET Core and should be used in server projects.
    Server projects should add: <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
    For client library builds, the hub base is excluded.
  -->

  <!-- Exclude server-side hub components from client builds - they require ASP.NET Core SignalR -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="ServerSync/SecureStoreHubBase.cs" />
    <Compile Remove="ServerSync/RateLimitingHubFilter.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Exclude Diagnostics Razor components from Release builds (DEBUG-only feature) -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)' != 'Debug'">
    <Content Remove="Diagnostics\Components\*.razor" />
    <Compile Remove="Diagnostics\Components\*.razor" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
